### 10.2 Supply Chain Security and CI Risks

Recent supply chain attacks, such as the Trivy GitHub Actions compromise, highlight the importance of pinning actions to full commit SHAs rather than version tags. Attackers have demonstrated the ability to force-update tags and inject malicious payloads, exposing CI/CD secrets and credentials. Best practices for C.H.A.D-os v1 include:

- Pinning all GitHub Actions to immutable commit SHAs.
- Regularly auditing workflows for compromised dependencies.
- Rotating secrets and credentials after any suspected compromise.
- Using artifact scanning tools (e.g., Trivy) with verified, trusted sources only.

